# Location-head weights. ONE glob, and it covers the ladder (v10 + v11) — v5's redundant
# literal line above it went out with v5's weight on 2026-08-08. The glob is deliberately
# left broad rather than narrowed to the two live versions: an LFS rule on a path with no
# file is inert, and the failure it prevents (a 34 MB .pt committed as a raw blob because
# someone added a version before editing this file) is the one that cannot be undone cheaply.
data/classifier/*/model_best.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/wallpaper_head/v3/model_best.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v4b's PINNED weight is seed 1's, not the top-level model_best.pt (seed 0). The seed
# was picked on best blind sheet-D AUC>=4 at the 2026-08-11 adoption; the rule names the
# exact file the pin resolves to, because that is the only .pt under v4b/ that is
# tracked and a broader glob would arm four weights nobody is committing.
data/wallpaper_head/v4b/seed_1/model_best.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v4 (the five-seed retrain, 2026-08-05 sitting folded in) had a rule here while it was a
# STAGED candidate. Its WEIGHT was DE-TRACKED on 2026-08-08: `wallpaper_pins` still pins v3,
# so under ACTIVE+PREVIOUS retention v4 is neither — it is a staged candidate that was never
# adopted, and the policy de-tracks those (storage_classes.md § weights retention). A
# verified emergency copy of the whole v4 tree, all five seeds included, sits unreferenced
# at <artifacts>/retired_weights/wallpaper_head_v4/.
#   CORRECTION (2026-08-08): this note used to say `metrics.json` was untracked "as it
#   always was". It is tracked, and so is `config.json` — they are the RUN RECORD the
#   retention policy explicitly keeps, which is what stops the rejection being
#   re-litigated. Both were force-added at a gitignored path and now carry exact-path
#   .gitignore negations. What IS untracked working state: the weight, the five per-seed
#   dirs, `eval_scores.jsonl`, `per_seed.json`, `inference.py`, the eval montage, train.log.
data/render_mode_head/v1/model_best.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v3 (the `dedup_weighted` arm) became the LIVE mining gate on 2026-08-11
# (prompts/flip_29.md); v1 stays as PREVIOUS. The four sibling arms (v3_aug, v3_augx,
# v3_uniform, v3_ap2) get NO rule: they are experiments, none is pinnable, and their
# weights stay untracked working state beside their tracked run records.
data/render_mode_head/v3/model_best.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v2 (the 2026-08-06 finetune of v1 on the 960-row rebuilt correction sheet) had an LFS rule
# here while it was a live candidate. It LOST the winner rule the same day — significantly
# worse at both >=2 boundaries — and a REJECTED candidate is not a critical final weight, so
# the rule went out together with the .gitignore negation and the canary/allowlist entries
# (prompts/mining_adoption_prompt.md §3). Its RUN RECORD stays tracked
# (data/render_mode_head/v2/{config,metrics,per_seed}.json + report.{md,json}), and the
# committed trainer + corpus + the recipe recorded in config.json reproduce it per-seed.
data/queries/scorer/v3_gvo/model_best.pt filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/discovery/**/harvest_log.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/discovery/**/prio_terms.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/discovery/**/maneuvers.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/discovery/**/q4_candidates.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# ...and their ROTATED SEGMENTS (`<stem>.<nnn>.jsonl.gz`, tools/run_record.py). This rule is
# what makes the compaction real rather than cosmetic: git zlib-compresses an ordinary blob
# already (committing maneuvers.jsonl raw and committing the same rows gzipped both pack to
# ~451 kB, measured 2026-08-07), so gzip only buys bytes where the object ships RAW — which
# is exactly the LFS path the four streams above take. One pattern rather than four because
# the segment suffix is the same for every stream and a per-stream rule would go stale the
# next time a stream joins `run_record.SEGMENTED_STREAMS`
# (`test_run_record.py::test_the_lfs_rules_cover_the_segments_of_every_lfs_tracked_stream`).
data/discovery/**/*.jsonl.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Frozen v7 eval slice: only a full GPU eval-freeze (classifier/train_v7.py) produces it
# and it's ignored by the blanket /data/* rule, so it must be force-added like the
# classifier weights. This ensures it lands in LFS when it is: `git add -f
# data/classifier/v7/eval_scores_v7.jsonl`. It's the frozen input the keeper calibration
# gate (tools/atlas/keeper_cut.py, test_steered_frontier.py) derives + tests against.
data/classifier/**/eval_scores_v7.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v8 build artifacts. Unlike v4..v7 (which wrote these to ignored, untracked paths and
# lost every one of them), the v8 population record is durable() and committed.
# manifest.jsonl / eval_slice.jsonl / build_metadata.json / aug_roster.json are small and
# stay plain text (readable in a diff, which is the point for a split assignment). These
# paths are NEGATED in .gitignore by exact path, so a normal `git add` works — no
# force-add needed, and `git check-ignore --no-index` confirms it independently of the
# index.
#   v8's plan.jsonl + cache_manifest.jsonl had LFS rules here until 2026-08-03, when both
#   files were deleted: 146 MB of rows that tools/v8/build_plan.py reproduces byte-for-byte
#   from the committed manifest. v9's pair followed on 2026-08-08 on the same argument, once
#   the recipe-parity gate that read it was retired with the aug-cache trees; v10's pair is
#   the one still tracked.
data/classifier/**/eval_scores_v8.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v9 build artifacts.
#   v9's plan.jsonl + cache_manifest.jsonl had LFS rules here until 2026-08-08, when both
#   files were deleted: 146 MB of rows that tools/v9/build_plan.py reproduces byte-for-byte
#   from data/v8/manifest.jsonl (measured — sha256 equal on both, 2026-08-08). They were
#   tracked to arm the v10 recipe-parity gate on a cache extension; the gate was retired the
#   same day along with data/v{9,10}/aug_cache. v10's pair followed hours later — see below.
data/classifier/**/eval_scores_v9.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
#   data/v9/eval_scores_v9.jsonl had an LFS rule here for UNIFORMITY with v10's and v11's,
#   not for its size (281 KB). It was removed 2026-08-08 with the pair above: LFS is not a
#   side door, so tests/test_large_tracked_blobs.py requires every LFS-tracked path to sit
#   under an allowlist entry that covers something over 1 MiB, and once v9's plan and
#   cache_manifest went there was nothing large left under data/v9/ to hang the exception
#   on. A 281 KB text file in plain git is the honest answer; the uniformity argument was
#   uniformity with two files that no longer exist.
# v10 build artifacts.
#   v10's plan.jsonl + cache_manifest.jsonl had LFS rules here until 2026-08-08, when both
#   files were deleted: 179 MB (201,168 rows each) that tools/v10/build_plan.py reproduces
#   byte-for-byte from data/v10/manifest.jsonl plus v9's committed roster and colormaps
#   (measured — sha256 equal on both, 2026-08-08). They were tracked because they were the
#   only thing mapping a cached tile back to a location; data/v{9,10}/aug_cache was deleted
#   earlier the same day, so there is no tile left to map. All three of v8/v9/v10 have now
#   made the same move for the same reason, which is the pattern rather than three
#   coincidences: a DERIVED row file is not a record, the manifest it derives from is.
#   data/v10/eval_scores_v10.jsonl keeps its rule — at 293 KB it is under the 1 MiB bar like
#   v9's was, but unlike v9's it still has something over the bar under data/v10/ to hang its
#   allowlist entry on (manifest.jsonl, 2.2 MB), so nothing forces it plain.
data/v10/eval_scores_v10.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# v11's frozen eval slice. v11 commits NO plan/cache_manifest pair — both are bulk and
# out-of-tree (.gitignore, and artifacts._is_v11_build_rows) — so this is the only v11 row
# file with an LFS rule, and at 1.4 MB it is the only one of the three that earns the rule
# on its own SIZE — v10's now rides data/v10/manifest.jsonl (its big pair went 2026-08-08)
# and v9's went plain the same day, so `data/v<N>/eval_scores_<N>.jsonl` is no longer
# uniform and no longer should be.
# The weight itself needs no line: the
# `data/classifier/*/model_best.pt` glob above already covers v11.
data/v11/eval_scores_v11.jsonl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
